CPU / boot: arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8939.dtsi:41 onward defines eight
spin-table CPUs with zero placeholder cpu-release-addr values and a second-stage
shim requirement. MPIDRs are0x100..103 and0..3; boot CPU is0x100.
Documentation/arch/arm64/booting.rst and arch/arm64/kernel/smp_spin_table.c
define the actual handoff. This is not equivalent to downstream
qcom,arm-cortex-acc. Pocketboot source 79cdf784c476be70f7f58cd73b37dfaeb0bf1c6f
has only the four-core MSM8916 v1 contract; its separate repository evidence
note pins qhypstub and both relevant lk2nd branches. EL2 is not a prerequisite
for this source inventory, and Android unlocking does not prove firmware fuses.

